# TypeScript standards

Follow these skills for all work in `apps/web/src`:

- `.agents/skills/typescript-jsdoc-style/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/typescript-solid-design/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/typescript-project-structure/SKILL.md`

## Non-negotiables

- No component-layer barrel files under `components/`
- Folder-per-component layout with direct imports
- Page-only Reachability code under `pages/Reachability/{components,constants,utils,types,services}/`
- Top-level `constants/` (`mapbox.constants.ts` only) and `utils/` (DateTimePicker helpers only)
- Exported APIs use well-formed JSDoc with verb-phrase summaries for components
- `utils/` and `constants/` must not import component `index.types`
- Depend on service ports from `types/`, wire concretes only in `services/app-services.ts`
- Pure helpers belong in `utils/` or `pages/<Page>/utils/`, not loose files under `components/**`

Run `pnpm validate:skills` before finishing TypeScript changes.

See task routing in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) for domain and workflow skills.
